  "description": "Dense full 7x7 BGA-49 0.8mm: inner 5x5 all signals to far headers, perimeter GND/VCC planes, 8-layer. The genuine inner-ball-escape vehicle the rest of the corpus lacks (every other dense BGA here is 4-layer, so its inner pair are planes with no signal layer to escape onto). The structured via-in-pad escape to inner signal layers routes the inner balls F/B cannot reach: ~7% complete without it, ~33% with. The remaining ceiling is the per-ring channel limit at 0.8mm (one trace between barrels) \u2014 an angular-corridor escape would lift it; not a fault.",
